[ Note : We encourage CFPB to utilize its XXXX XXXX to obtain these and other relevant communications from Intercoastal ] We also believe that Intercoastal acted in bad faith when XXXX and XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, after we notified Intercoastal that we terminated XXXX & XXXX, committed to work with us to move forward and transfer our loan to a new builder. On more than XXXX occasion, including in conversations with our attorney, XXXX committed to helping us move forward. Instead, less than a month later, Intercoastal sent us a Notice XXXX XXXX and despite CEO XXXX XXXX XXXX to help us find a positive way forward, in the end, Intercoastal had no real desire to help us. XXXX separate mortgage lenders we contacted, as we searched for alternative lending, expressed surprise that XXXX would take such steps and stated such action would be unusual and questioned whether there XXXX have been something to hide. By the time XXXX sent its final letter, via outside attorney, reiterating its intent to terminate the loan, we were left with little time to obtain new financing. In the end, we were forced to sell our property at a loss to pay off the construction loan with XXXX. 

Background : On XX/XX/XXXX, our realtor contacted XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, the realtor representing XXXX and XXXX & XXXX Builders, concerning construction of a new home on a property in XXXX, XXXX A subsequent email from XXXX to our realtor specified that I did speak with the builder and Intercoastal Mortgage XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, XXXX ) is the required lender for the construction to permanent loan. 

